---
layout: changelog
title: "Change what a custom domain serves without adding it again"
date: 2026-11-24
cover: /images/blog/announcing-domain-updates/cover.avif
tags: sites, functions, domains, console, api
---

You can now [update a domain](/docs/products/sites/domains#update-a-domain) on Appwrite Sites and Functions. Click **Update** in a domain's menu on the **Domains** tab to switch it between the active deployment and a branch, pick a different branch, or change a redirect's URL and status code. The domain keeps its DNS records and certificate, so nothing changes at your DNS provider.

A domain can't switch between serving a deployment and redirecting, and Appwrite refuses to move a domain to a branch with no successful deployment. From your server, `updateSiteRule`, `updateFunctionRule`, and `updateRedirectRule` on the Proxy service make the same changes and can also move a domain to another site or function in the same project.

